# Default-deny policy for .claude/.
# Nothing here is committed unless explicitly whitelisted below.
#
# Rationale: .claude/ holds a mix of per-user state (settings.local.json,
# personal skills, session droppings) and occasionally things you want
# shared with collaborators (a team /deploy command, a project-specific
# agent). Default-deny + explicit whitelist makes "shared" opt-in.

*
!.gitignore

# --- Whitelist shared items below by uncommenting / adding ---

# Shared skills (project-scoped commands like /deploy, /release):
# !skills/
# !skills/<skill-name>/
# !skills/<skill-name>/**

# Shared project commands:
# !commands/
# !commands/**

# Shared project agents:
# !agents/
# !agents/**

# Team-shared settings (NOT settings.local.json — that's per-user):
# !settings.json
